.\n- **What the bill does:** Section 220.5 bars schools and their boards from any policy that \"would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That is rung 2's wording.\n- **Why not the neighbouring rungs:** The bill does not require staff to keep the information from parents, so it is not rung 1. It does not require telling parents in any case, so it is not rungs 3 to 5.\n- **Timing:** The vote falls inside his current Assembly term, which began 2022-12-05.\n- **Which vote I used:** The earlier Assembly floor vote of 2024-04-25 was on a different, older text of the bill. I left it out.\n\nThe chair rests on two passages for this one vote: the vote page and the chaptered bill text. Both count as a single source, so it will be tiered `single-source`. No passage contains his own words, so there are no candidate quotes, and nothing is listed under `needs_source`.\n\nThe file is at `/Users/chrisandrews/Documents/GitHub/ev-accounts-egi-la/backend/data/stance-research/2026-10-13-egi-a1v2-la/mike-a-gipson/labels/coder-1.json`.","ttft_ms":14828,"type":"result","duration_ms":32870,"uuid":"f31cabac-411a-4828-9f1b-5b4200e4cb51","ttft_stream_ms":7639,"time_to_request_ms":304,"first_content_frame_ms":7640,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
